dmrcrack (0.4.0+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.0.
  * Refuse to brute-force unsupported ciphers (AES): the engine now classifies
    the capture up front and aborts on non-RC4 traffic instead of running a full
    keyspace scan and reporting a junk key.
  * Fix an out-of-bounds read in precompute_cipher_packs on payloads shorter
    than 33 bytes (CPU and OpenCL host paths).
  * Single-source the DMR de-interleave tables in include/dmr_tables.h.

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dmrcrack (0.3.3+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package.
  * Build the portable CPU-only engine (no CUDA/HIP build dependency) so the
    package builds with a free toolchain on the Debian/Kali autobuilders.
  * Repack the upstream tarball (+dfsg) to drop the prebuilt Windows-only
    WinSparkle binaries (see debian/copyright Files-Excluded).

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Mon, 01 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
